"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h1>Formal Proof</h1>\n<h2>Problem Statement</h2>\n<p>Solve for x: 3x + 7 = 22</p>\n<h2>Goal</h2>\n<p>Find the value of x</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>Proof</h2>\n<p><strong>Step 0</strong> (algebraic):</p>\n<p>$$3x + 7 = 22$$</p>\n<p>Restate the linear equation 3x + 7 = 22 and identify x as the variable to be solved.</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Given problem statement</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Initial state of the equation where x is the unknown variable in the domain of real numbers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Step 1</strong> (algebraic):</p>\n<p>$$3x + 7 - 7 = 22 - 7$$</p>\n<p>Subtract 7 from both sides of the equation to isolate the term containing x.</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Subtraction Property of Equality, which states that if $a = b$, then $a - c = b - c$.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong> (simplification):</p>\n<p>$$3x = 15$$</p>\n<p>Simplify both sides of the equation by performing the subtraction.</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Arithmetic simplification of the terms on both sides of the equation ($7 - 7 = 0$ and $22 - 7 = 15$).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3</strong> (algebraic):</p>\n<p>$$\\frac{3x}{3} = \\frac{15}{3}$$</p>\n<p>Divide both sides of the equation by 3 to isolate the variable x.</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Division Property of Equality, which states that if $a = b$ and $c \\neq 0$, then $\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{b}{c}$.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 4</strong> (simplification):</p>\n<p>$$x = 5$$</p>\n<p>Simplify both sides of the equation to find the value of x.</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Arithmetic simplification of the terms on both sides of the equation (\\frac{3}{3} = 1 and \\frac{15}{3} = 5).</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<p>$$x = 5$$</p>\n<p><strong>Q.E.D.</strong> ∎</p>\n<hr />\n<p><em>Proof completed in 5 steps with 100% confidence.</em></p>\n</div></div><div><div class=\" completion-message response-message\"></div></div>"